GUI modernization, Phase 5 (fifth slice): Incidents master/detail - the
remaining half of "Rebuild Incidents (master/detail, search/sort/filter)"
deliberately deferred from the search/sort/filter slice. Closes that
Phase 5 line.

## 1. A new shell primitive had to exist first

The execution order's shell diagram (§4.1) names an "optional
InspectorPanel (becomes a drawer under 900px width)" inside
`WorkspaceBody`, meant as a general primitive other investigation pages
would reuse, not an Incidents-specific concern - confirmed by grepping
for it before assuming it already existed: `InspectorPanel` was named
only in planning prose, with zero implementation anywhere in
`desktop/src`.

The named design - a true modal drawer under 900px, with a focus trap -
was scaled back deliberately. This project's own sidebar work already
documents the same kind of deferral for the same reason
(`App.css`'s `@media (max-width: 899px)` block: "Not yet an icon rail...
needs the icon system Phase 2 adds"): a fully-correct focus-trapped modal
needs verification this environment cannot fully provide (no screen
reader here, and axe-core's automated rules do not exercise dynamic
focus-trap/keyboard-modal behaviour at all - proven directly in §4
below, not assumed). `InspectorPanel` is instead a non-modal `role=
"region"` that CSS docks beside the list at >=900px and stacks below it
under that (reusing the existing 899px breakpoint rather than inventing
a second one) - it never covers or hides the list, so there is no focus
trap to get wrong because nothing is ever made inert. Upgrading to a true
drawer is tracked as a separate, later piece of work, once the icon-rail
work gives this project a real verified pattern for it.

## 2. What was built

`InspectorPanel.tsx` (new): title, a close button (`IconButton`,
labelled), children. `Incidents.tsx`: `IncidentRow` (a compact,
single-line summary - time, severity, translated title, confidence -
deliberately without the chain/evidence/advice detail `IncidentCard`
carries, so the list is genuinely more scannable, not the same content
at a smaller font). Master/detail is opt-in, entered by selecting a row
or a new small "show in a side panel" link under each full card:

- Nothing selected (the default, and the state every pre-existing test
  was written against): renders exactly as before this slice, every
  filtered incident as a full `IncidentCard` - zero regression, and
  proven by every one of the 17 pre-existing Incidents tests still
  passing completely unchanged.
- A selection present and still among the filtered incidents: the
  compact list plus the `InspectorPanel` showing that one incident's
  full `IncidentCard` (evidence disclosures, export button, everything
  the last three slices built, all still working inside the panel).
- A selection present but stale (filtered out, or an id that never
  matched anything): falls back to the default full-card list rather
  than showing nothing or crashing - the same "never blank, never a
  crash" discipline applied to a routing edge case instead of a
  translation one.

Selection reuses `InvestigationContext.selection` - not a new field -
the same one the previous slice's export flow already writes when
navigating to Evidence (with `from`/`to` alongside it there; here alone,
without them, distinguishing "show this incident's detail on this same
page" from "export this incident on a different page" by which fields
are set together, not by inventing a second field for a very similar
idea).

